    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 0,
        "text": "Dawn on 2 December 1805, a year to the day after the coronation. Fog fills the valleys. Napoleon has about 73,000 men; the Russian and Austrian emperors about 85,000."
      },
      {
        "t": 0.5,
        "text": "The allies mean to turn the French right. Three columns march down off the Pratzen Heights towards Telnitz and Sokolnitz, where Napoleon has deliberately left few troops."
      },
      {
        "t": 1.2,
        "text": "Davout's men, after marching about 110 km from Vienna in two days, arrive just in time to hold the villages on the Goldbach stream."
      },
      {
        "t": 2,
        "text": "About 9 o'clock the sun breaks through. Soult's divisions, hidden in the mist below, climb the Pratzen. The allied centre is almost empty."
      },
      {
        "t": 3.2,
        "text": "Kolowrat's and Miloradovich's column is caught on the march. After two hours of hard fighting the French hold the heights."
      },
      {
        "t": 4.6,
        "text": "In the north Lannes and Murat's heavy cavalry fight Bagration and Prince Liechtenstein's horsemen along the Brünn road."
      },
      {
        "t": 5.6,
        "text": "Around 1 pm the Russian Imperial Guard counter-attacks near Staré Vinohrady. Napoleon's Guard cavalry under Bessières and Rapp throws it back."
      },
      {
        "t": 7,
        "text": "Now the French turn south. The three allied columns at Telnitz and Sokolnitz are attacked from behind as well as in front."
      },
      {
        "t": 8.2,
        "text": "They break. Przhebyshevsky's column surrenders. Others flee across the frozen Satschan ponds. Legend says French guns broke the ice and thousands drowned; when the ponds were drained, only a few bodies were found."
      },
      {
        "t": 9.4,
        "text": "By dusk the allies have lost about 27,000 men killed, wounded or captured, and some 180 guns. The French lost about 9,000. Two days later Emperor Francis asks for an armistice."
      }
    ]
  },
